@workspace

We already built docs/reconciliation-architecture-viewer.html.

Now add a ChatGPT-like AI assistant to the Code2Arch architecture viewer.

Important:
Do NOT call GitHub Models or Copilot model APIs directly from browser JavaScript because the GitHub token must not be exposed.

Implement a small backend API that the HTML page can call.

Required architecture:

1. Frontend:
   docs/reconciliation-architecture-viewer.html

2. Backend:
   server/code2arch-assistant-server.js

3. Environment:
   GITHUB_TOKEN must be read from process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN
   MODEL_NAME must be read from process.env.MODEL_NAME
   Default model can be openai/gpt-4.1-mini

4. Backend endpoint:
   POST /api/chat

5. Request payload from frontend:
   {
     "question": "user question",
     "selectedNode": {...},
     "architectureContext": {...}
   }

6. Backend behavior:
   - Receive user question
   - Load architecture model from docs/architecture-model.json if available
   - Combine:
     user question
     selected node
     relevant architecture model context
   - Send prompt to GitHub Models chat completions API
   - Return the assistant response to frontend

7. GitHub Models endpoint:
   POST https://models.github.ai/inference/chat/completions

8. Headers:
   Authorization: Bearer ${GITHUB_TOKEN}
   Content-Type: application/json

9. Body:
   {
     "model": process.env.MODEL_NAME || "openai/gpt-4.1-mini",
     "messages": [
       {
         "role": "system",
         "content": "You are Code2Arch AI Assistant. Explain enterprise Scala/Spark reconciliation architecture using only the provided architecture model. If something is unknown, say UNKNOWN. Do not hallucinate."
       },
       {
         "role": "user",
         "content": "<question + selected node + relevant architecture context>"
       }
     ],
     "temperature": 0.2,
     "max_tokens": 1200
   }

